# training-ground

PyTorch training (not scaffolded). Consumes JSON dumps, trains the cubeless net, exports ONNX for `game-engine`.

- Positions: JSON in `docs/domain/board-representation.md`. Inputs: tensor in `docs/domain/features.md`. Labels: cubeless probs in `docs/domain/evaluation.md`.
- Implement the same 206-float featurizer as TypeScript; test against golden fixtures.
- Checkpoints, `wandb/`, `*.pt`, and `*.onnx` are gitignored. Do not commit them.
- Do not add `pyproject.toml` unless the user asks.
- Docker only, from `training-ground/`: `docker compose run --rm train python -m pytest` (when tests exist); training via `docker compose run --rm train <command>`. IDE `.venv`: `docker compose --profile install-host run --rm install-host` (no-op until `pyproject.toml` or `requirements.txt` exists; Linux venv is not a host interpreter). Do not run host `python` / `pip`. Data layout is still open.
